ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":80,"prev":82,"next":84,"titles":87,"firmware":36},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":26,"procedures":60,"parameters":61,"related":62,"body":68,"sources":69,"official_url":30,"controls":79},"com.usb","USB connections",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"usb","usb-c","usb midi","usb audio","usb host","class compliant","powered hub","com",35,"knowledge/manual/units/com/usb.md",{"modes":16,"screens":17},[],[],"The USB-C port works both ways. A computer sees a driverless audio and MIDI device; as a host the OP-XY accepts class-compliant MIDI gear and audio interfaces plugged into it.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[23],"1.1.32","1.1.15",null,[27,32,38,42,45,49,53,57],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"both-ways","The USB-C port carries audio and MIDI as a USB device (to a computer) and as a USB host (for gear plugged into the OP-XY).","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/hardware-overview#technical-specifications","official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":35,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":36,"confidence":37},"class-compliant","A computer sees the OP-XY as a class-compliant USB audio and MIDI device, so no driver is needed; its one MIDI input and one MIDI output are both named OP-XY.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--first-contact-read-only","1.1.33","verified",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":41,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":36,"confidence":37},"audio-to-computer","The computer can record the OP-XY's output as a stereo USB audio input at 44.1 kHz and 16 bit.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":35,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":36,"confidence":37},"audio-from-computer","The USB link also offers an audio stream from the computer into the OP-XY; that it arrives as the external audio track's usb audio input is likely but not confirmed.",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":48,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"host-gear","USB MIDI keyboards, controllers and synths plug straight into the OP-XY through a USB-C cable or adapter, with no computer involved; a powered hub helps gear that needs more power.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#how-to-control-op-xy",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":52,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"interfaces","Audio interfaces work when they are USB audio class 1 or 2 compliant; ones that need a driver may not.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#use-an-audio-interface-with-op-xy",{"id":54,"text":55,"source":56,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"start-fix","OS 1.1.32 fixed the unit sometimes failing to start while connected to USB.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.32",{"id":58,"text":59,"source":41,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":36,"confidence":37},"mtp-switch","In MTP mode the computer sees a file-transfer device instead, so USB audio and MIDI are gone until MTP ends.",[],[],[63,64,65,66,67],"hardware.connectors","com.devices","com.mtp","howto.midi-keyboard","howto.audio-interface","With a computer, one cable carries MIDI and audio in both directions — this app uses it to play and\nhear the OP-XY. With other gear, the OP-XY is the host.",[70,72,74,75,76,77],{"url":30,"kind":71},"guide",{"url":35,"kind":73},"research",{"url":41,"kind":73},{"url":48,"kind":71},{"url":52,"kind":71},{"url":56,"kind":78},"changelog",[],{"id":12,"title":81},"Connectivity",{"id":64,"title":83},"Connected MIDI devices",{"id":85,"title":86},"com.controller-mode","MIDI controller mode",{"basics.key-notation":88,"basics.main-modes":89,"basics.modules":90,"basics.track-buttons":91,"basics.linked-tracks":92,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":93,"basics.workflow":94,"basics.firmware-versions":95,"hardware.layout":96,"hardware.power-and-charging